[size=4][i]Beat me up for science.[/i][/size]

[size=5][b]Description[/b][/size]

Immortal training dummies for testing damage, healing, auras, and hit logging. Summon them, tune their level and health, set them Enemy so harmful effects land, and watch a live combat log with DPS and HPS graphs while you go to town.

Both male and female use EncBandit Nord bases. Up to three of each gender can be out at once. They stay put (handy for RaceMenu and overlay redraws), keep template outfits for SPID and outfit distributors, and hitting them does not count as assault — town guards stay out of it.

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/96817]SKSE Menu Framework[/url]
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/180775]Magic Tattoos Framework[/url] and friends, if that is what you are testing. Enemy / Archnemesis faction checks for Cast an aura needs MTF Plugin - Skyrim 0.3.3+
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Install with your mod manager and enable [font=Courier New]PTX_TrainingDummy.esp[/font]. Open the Mod Control Panel (Menu Framework hotkey) → [b]Training Dummy[/b], or the standalone window from that section. The quest adds the three summon / dismiss spells on first load.

[size=5][b]Spells[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Summon Male / Female Training Dummy[/b] — places another dummy in front of you (up to 3 per gender; refuses when full)
[*][b]Dismiss Training Dummy[/b] — removes all live dummies
[/list]

[size=5][b]SKSE UI[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Summon / dismiss / heal now
[*][b]Match player level[/b] (default on), or a fixed level
[*][b]Health per level[/b] (default 50): max HP = level × this
[*][b]Start at % HP[/b] (default 100): useful for testing healing auras
[*][b]vs player[/b] relationship (default Lover): set [b]Enemy[/b] or [b]Archnemesis[/b] so harmful Cast an aura hits them
[*]Rolling combat log with 5s / 10s DPS and HPS graphs, clear, and copy to clipboard
[/list]

Settings live in [font=Courier New]Data/SKSE/Plugins/TrainingDummyUI/settings.json[/font]. Hits are also appended to [font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/Logs/Script/User/TrainingDummy.log[/font].

[size=5][b]Credits[/b][/size]

Built for use with Magic Tattoos Framework. SKSE Menu Framework for the UI.
